The Miyami Rebellion ({{nihongo|Miyami Souran|宮美争乱}}), also called the Tachikawa Rebellion was a civil war that occurred in [[Nakamizu]] during [[Kawaei Shogunate]] period. It started by the succession dispute from [[Emperor Yonmyo]] to [[Princess Miya]] following his death in 1796. It is indirectly caused by the progressive modernization by Kawaei Shogunate administration in late 18th century triggers the conservative faction of Kawaei Shogunate government. 
