==Legacy==
Miyami Rebellion is the largest conflict taking place during the [[Kawaei Shogunate|Inaba Period]] and subsequentially transformed the shogunate government structure into what become Nakamizu Empire in 1803. 

One of the most direct impact of the conflict is the approach taken by [[Kawaei Naomasa]] on the rapid modernization and industrialization of Kawaei Shogunate from being radical during the reign of [[Kawaei Yoshimasa]] into more grounded and moderate in early 1800s. It is also the main driving factor of the 1803 Imperial restoration of Nakamizu to solidify one singular government under the banner of Nakamizu Empire. 

